  "messages" : [ {
    "role" : "system",
    "content" : "[[hc-role-prompt]]\nYou are Plan. Your sole persistent deliverable is the user-visible draft\nat `plans/<name>.md` in the master worktree, never inside an internal state\ndirectory. Choose `<name>`: descriptive, `[a-z0-9-]`, at most 80 characters,\nunique. The system rejects unsafe or duplicate names. The first accepted\n`write` fixes the path; a different path is refused.\n\n# Milestones (S1 -> S2 -> S3 -> 待执行)\n- S1 (Requirements Analysis): Apply the methods of Ronald A. Howard,\n  Raymond Thomas Dalio, and Jeff Bezos until nothing remains to improve.\n- S2 (Implementation Skeleton): Apply the methods of George Polya and Alan\n  H. Schoenfeld to explore the optimal implementation skeleton and key\n  points until nothing remains to improve.\n- S3 (Parallel Development Methodology): Using Donald Knuth-style\n  pseudocode, specify the development methodology that maximizes concurrent\n  developers and minimizes wall-clock time until nothing remains to improve.\n- 待执行 (Ready for Execution): The draft is finalized for handoff.\nMilestone judgment rule: each stage judges only the gap to starting the next\nstage (S1 -> can S2 start; S2 -> can S3 start; S3 -> can execution start).\nNever count next-stage work as a current-stage gap.\n\n# Surface (`clj-plan`) and read/write boundary\nSubmit one `(defprogram <name> [] ...)` form using EDN + UFSS literals\n(`#\"...\"#`, `#\"\"\"...\"\"\"#`). Every capability is a bare function with one\nEDN map; there is no `this` and no positional argument.\n- `(cat {:path ...})` reads only the draft and operator attachments.\n- `(write {:path ... :content ...})` writes only the draft. It is refused\n  `:WRITE_LOCKED_BEFORE_FIRST_REVIEW` until your first accepted `review` in\n  this tenure; a new tenure locks it again, and after handoff the draft is\n  frozen (`:DRAFT_LOCKED_AFTER_HANDOFF`).\n- The operator may edit the draft file on disk at any time; `cat` before\n  `write` when refining, and on `:FILE_CONFLICT` or `:DRAFT_USER_EDITED`\n  re-read the file and rewrite the polished version — the disk content is\n  authoritative.\n- `(where {:content ... :needle ...})` and\n  `(whereAll {:content ... :needle ...})` find exact text.\n- `(park {:payload ...})` and `(unpark {:name ... :value ...})` suspend and\n  resume this program.\n- `(ask {:question ...})` is available only in S1. It is\n  `(park {:payload {:question ...}})` plus a turn interrupt; outside S1 it is\n  refused `:ASK_FORBIDDEN_OUTSIDE_S1`.\n- `(devops {:verbose-intent \"...\"})` synchronously joins the one Plan\n  dedicated worker for this tenure and returns its final report verbatim as\n  `{:status :ok|:failed|:interrupted :report \"...\"}`. Reuse or steer that\n  worker; never create a second investigation path.\n- `(review {:findings [...]})` submits the obligation ledger\n  `[{:key k :value v-or-nil} ...]`. In the Plan phase a non-empty ledger is\n  yours to service by editing the draft; no Swarm starts. Clear a serviced\n  key with `{:key k :value nil}`; an empty vector alone does not clear an\n  open ledger. On the initial S1 tenure's first empty review, the system asks\n  `我需要干什么？` instead of recording the review; resume with\n  `(unpark ...)`. In `待执行`, non-empty findings are refused\n  `:NONEMPTY_FINDINGS_AT_PENDING`, and an open ledger must be cleared first\n  (`:NONEMPTY_LEDGER_AT_PENDING`); an empty review is the only handoff and\n  starts execution from the saved draft bytes without ending this Plan\n  tenure. A missing or empty draft is refused `:DRAFT_MISSING_OR_EMPTY`\n  before any execution tenure exists.\nThere is no shell, `call`, `eval`, stat/ls, board, or token capability in\n`clj-plan`. Investigate repository facts only through `(devops ...)`.\n\nThe system is always authorized and unattended. The only legal stops are a\nparked `(ask ...)` in S1 and the `待执行` handoff. Otherwise the guard injects\na Nudge with the open ledger (or the unreviewed milestone) and requires you\nto continue.\n\n# Scope\nEvery tool call carries flat `:scope` (`:reset-scope` with\n`:new-scope-goal` and `:new-scope-retention-budget`, `:keep-last`,\n`:remove-last` with `:replacement`, or `:me-too`). One true annotation per\nmodel turn; an all-`:me-too` turn defaults to `:keep-last`; budget 0 admits\nonly `:reset-scope`; after restart, initialize with `:reset-scope`\n(`:SCOPE_UNINITIALIZED`)."
  }, {
    "role" : "user",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "E2E06 OCR 检查 E2E06-1794222030269：请总结材料并引用页码。"
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "\n\n[Attachment: scan-3pages.pdf]\n第 1 页：\n部署检查清单 : ARS OMA. E2E06 page one.\n\n第 3 页：\n第二页扫描件 : 附加说明。 E2E06 page three."
    } ]
  }, {
    "role" : "assistant",
    "tool_calls" : [ {
      "id" : "pair-hint-815f4cb862d0aa9c",
      "type" : "function",
      "function" : {
        "name" : "",
        "arguments" : "{}"
      }
    } ]
  }, {
    "role" : "tool",
    "tool_call_id" : "pair-hint-815f4cb862d0aa9c",
    "content" : "Reasoning and all outward output must be in English.\n\n# Pair programming discipline\nMnemonic: every job has an owner and every change leaves a record; forks are never settled by the clock; verification buys only the difference and must show red; boundaries are authority and intent outranks wording; facts must prove their provenance; land small steps early and never skimp on the whole; history is not state, only independent work runs in parallel, and batches are never worshipped; be certain as under oath, change the horse not the rider, split the lanes not the account; a return is only testimony and convergence beats arrival; leave work that can be continued and think before you speak; memory is not government, defeat does not erase cause, stopping needs a reason, leave no cruft, and keep an inward ledger.\nTool names, parameter names, keywords, enum literals, file paths, and shell commands stay exactly as written; never translate them.\n\n# Token economy\nA prefix-cache hit reuses the unchanged head of a request. One changed byte before the tail forces recomputation of everything after it. Append facts; do not rewrite settled history. Cache hits are best-effort, never a guarantee.\n\n# Wait cost\nWaiting is not free. Send independent work out first, collect whatever has returned, and never idle for a whole batch. Calibrate against wall clock: unknown.\n\n# Context limit\nThe provider declares a context window of unknown. This is a fact, not a prediction. The system does not auto-compact on your behalf.\n\n# Budget calibration\nTurns spent: unknown. Estimated turns remaining: unknown. Wall clock used: unknown. These are calibration facts, not a hard execution limit.\n\n# Idle hint\nUnsettled .park handles: []. State explicitly how each handle will be settled. The system never resumes them for you.\n\n# Board observation\n[]\n\n# Fleet observation\n{:fleet-version 0 :swarms () :events []}\n"
  } ],
  "stream" : true,
  "stream_options" : {
    "include_usage" : true
  },
  "max_tokens" : 2048,
  "tools" : [ {
    "type" : "function",
    "function" : {
      "name" : "devops",
      "description" : "Run the Plan dedicated worker synchronously on the task model and return its full report.  The worker is read-only and is reused across calls in this tenure. Every call carries the flat :scope annotation.",
      "parameters" : {
        "type" : "object",
        "properties" : {
          "scope" : {
            "type" : "object",
            "description" : "Flat Scope annotation for this turn; see # Scope in the system prompt.",
            "properties" : {
              "kind" : {
                "type" : "string",
                "enum" : [ "reset-scope", "keep-last", "remove-last", "me-too" ]
              },
              "new-scope-goal" : {
                "type" : "string"
              },
              "new-scope-retention-budget" : {
                "minimum" : 1,
                "type" : "integer"
              },
              "replacement" : {
                "type" : "string"
              }
            },
            "required" : [ "kind" ]
          },
          "verbose-intent" : {
            "type" : "string"
          }
        },
        "required" : [ "verbose-intent", "scope" ]
      }
    }
  }, {
    "type" : "function",
    "function" : {
      "name" : "clj-plan",
      "description" : "Run one Plan program. The source must be one (defprogram ...) form using cat, write, where, whereAll, park, unpark, ask (S1 only), devops, and the top-level (review {:findings [...]}) primitive. Only the plans/<name>.md draft is writable, and only after the first accepted review in this tenure. There is no shell, call, eval, stat/ls, board, or token capability; investigate repository facts only through devops.",
      "parameters" : {
        "type" : "object",
        "properties" : {
          "intent" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Why this planning step runs and what result it produces."
          },
          "scope" : {
            "type" : "object",
            "description" : "Flat Scope annotation for this turn; see # Scope in the system prompt.",
            "properties" : {
              "kind" : {
                "type" : "string",
                "enum" : [ "reset-scope", "keep-last", "remove-last", "me-too" ]
              },
              "new-scope-goal" : {
                "type" : "string"
              },
              "new-scope-retention-budget" : {
                "minimum" : 1,
                "type" : "integer"
              },
              "replacement" : {
                "type" : "string"
              }
            },
            "required" : [ "kind" ]
          },
          "source" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "One (defprogram <name> [] ...) form in EDN+UFSS."
          }
        },
        "required" : [ "source", "intent", "scope" ]
      }
    }
  } ]
}
